[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The beads-migration plan's backlog register

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-BACKLOG-BEADS-MIGRATION
TITLE: The beads-migration plan's backlog register
DEPTH: interface-settled
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The linchpin every ungroomed item in this plan points at. An item is in the
backlog when it carries Backlogged_In to this node, and the plan's backlog is
the inbound Backlogs set.

This node holds no list. The edges are the list.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
One register per plan, so that the backlog is scoped the way the plan is and no
edge has to cross a plan boundary to reach it. This plan carries one ungroomed
item today, which does not make the register optional: an item with nothing to
attach to is exactly the case the edge exists to prevent.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Created 2026-08-27 alongside the equivalent register in the strictdoc-tooling
plan. The reasoning behind the shape is recorded there and is deliberately not
cited across the plan boundary, since INV-NO-EXTERNAL-PLAN-REFS is what keeps a
plan collectable.
<<<
